{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0121HqU41YGNNssiC5cQ9rAS","type":"tool_result","content":"    25\t| Order | manager | paid, small |\n    26\t| Dispatch | manager | free |\n    27\t| Observe | manager | paid, small |\n    28\t| Correct | manager | paid, small |\n    29\t| Read, edit, test, document | appliance | free |\n    30\t\n    31\t---\n    32\t\n    33\t## 1. Preflight — the gate\n    34\t\n    35\tNothing is dispatched until this passes.\n    36\t\n    37\t```bash\n    38\tcd ~/.hermes/skills/mlops/tiiny-model-routing\n    39\tpython3 scripts/route_check.py --thinking off \"<the goal>\"\n    40\t```\n    41\t\n    42\tRead the **residency** line, not the tier line.\n    43\t\n    44\t| residency | what to do |\n    45\t|---|---|\n    46\t| `loaded` | dispatch it |\n    47\t| `NOT loaded` | do **not** force that tier — either load the model first, or drop the override and take the resident model |\n    48\t\n    49\t**A forced tier overrides residency.** `delegate_task(tier=...)` selects\n    50\tthe tier's first choice and sends it, without checking what is loaded. A\n    51\tmodel that is not resident answers 404; Hermes treats 404 as terminal; the\n    52\tchild falls back to the paid provider *invisibly*, with a good answer and\n    53\ta bill. The tier is a hint; residency is the constraint.\n    54\t\n    55\tPreflight is cheap. A silent fallback is not.\n    56\t\n    57\t---\n    58\t\n    59\t## 2. Box assignment\n    60\t\n    61\t| | provider | role |\n    62\t|---|---|---|\n    63\t| Box A | the one `TIINY_BASE_URL` points at | primary worker — the residency probe reads this box, so this is the box a tier must be resident on |\n    64\t| Box B | the other, by its own address and bearer | second worker |\n    65\t\n    66\t**One heavy child per box.** The NPU is one pool per appliance and each\n    67\tbox serves one generation-heavy stream. Two children on one box starve\n    68\teach other, and the failure mode is a *hang*, not an error — the device\n    69\tkeeps reporting healthy while it answers nothing. Two boxes give two\n    70\tgenuinely parallel free streams.\n    71\t\n    72\t**A load is a swap.** It evicts whatever was resident, including the\n    73\tgeneralist the next wave will want. Load deliberately, and restore\n    74\tdeliberately.\n    75\t\n    76\t### Make the box match the router, not the router match the box\n    77\t\n    78\tWhen you want a specialist and the router probes Box A, put the\n    79\tspecialist on **Box A**. Do not repoint `TIINY_BASE_URL`, and do not wait\n    80\tfor a restart.\n    81\t\n    82\t`TIINY_BASE_URL` is read from the environment when the plugin is\n    83\timported, so changing it only takes effect in a new process. That makes\n    84\t\"the specialist is downloaded on Box B\" look like a blocked path. It is\n    85\tnot. A model that is merely *downloaded* on Box A costs nothing to load,\n    86\tand once it is resident there `route_check.py` reports `loaded` and the\n    87\ttier routes to it with no config change at all.\n    88\t\n    89\tMeasured: downloading a 55% specialist took about 20 minutes (free, in\n    90\tthe background, while other work continued); loading it afterwards took\n    91\t20 seconds. The download is the slow part and it is unattended — start it\n    92\tearly, keep working, and switch the tier when it lands.\n    93\t\n    94\t### Each box has its own bearer, and the wrong one looks like a dead box\n    95\t\n    96\t```\n    97\tTIINY_API_KEY     -> Box A\n    98\tTIINY_API_KEY_2   -> Box B\n    99\t```\n   100\t\n   101\tPoint the controller at Box B without swapping the bearer and it answers\n   102\t`HTTP 401 {\"error\":\"auth_failed\"}`, which the controller reports as\n   103\t`device UNREACHABLE`. **That is a wrong key, not a down box**, and the\n   104\twrong conclusion from it is \"the second box cannot be used\". Confirm with\n   105\ta one-line `curl` to that box's `/v1/models` using its own bearer before\n   106\tsaying anything about reachability.\n   107\t\n   108\tEach box also needs its own lock, hold and plan files, or two agents\n   109\tfight over one lock:\n   110\t\n   111\t```bash\n   112\tset -a; . ~/.hermes/.env; set +a\n   113\tcd ~/.hermes/skills/mlops/tiiny-model-routing\n   114\tTIINY_API_KEY=\"$TIINY_API_KEY_2\" \\\n   115\tTIINY_DEVICE_ADDRESS=192.0.2.11 \\\n   116\tTIINY_BASE_URL=http://192.0.2.11/v1 \\\n   117\tTIINY_HOST=http://192.0.2.11 \\\n   118\tTIINY_LOCK_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-lock-b.json \\\n   119\tTIINY_HOLD_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-hold-b.json \\\n   120\tTIINY_PLAN_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-plan-b.json \\\n   121\tpython3 scripts/tiiny_ctl.py status\n   122\t```\n   123\t\n   124\tThe mesh is the simpler door for both boxes when one is in front of them:\n   125\t`POST /mesh/lifecycle` with `action: start|stop|download` and a `target`.\n   126\t\n   127\t---\n   128\t\n   129\t## 3. The work order\n   130\t\n   131\tCopy [../templates/work-order.md](../templates/work-order.md) and fill it\n   132\tin. Every order carries:\n   133\t\n   134\t- **one job, one file.** No multi-file refactors in a single order.\n   135\t- **exact absolute paths.** Never a relative path the child has to guess.\n   200\t- **Run the acceptance command yourself.** A child that says the tests\n   201\t  pass has not run your tests.\n   202\t- **A child that verifies by string-matching has not verified.** A sweep\n   203\t  that rewrites paths will report \"N references rewritten, all resolve\"\n   204\t  after checking that each new path *string* is present in the file — which\n   205\t  passes even when the path does not resolve from that file's own\n   206\t  directory. Make the acceptance check **resolve the path**: join it\n   207\t  against the directory of the file that holds it and assert the target\n   208\t  exists. A relative path is only correct relative to something, and\n   209\t  `../` depth is the thing a rewrite gets wrong: a file two levels below\n   210\t  the root needs `../../`, and both `../` and `../../../` look plausible\n   211\t  in the source.\n   212\t- **A rewrite that changes what a sentence says is a corruption, not a\n   213\t  fix.** Path tokens appear inside prose that *describes* a path — \"the\n   214\t  design system links to `../brand/tap-monogram.png`\" — and rewriting\n   215\t  that mention to a vault-absolute path breaks the sentence's claim\n   216\t  while looking like a repair. After a bulk rewrite, read the changed\n   217\t  lines in context: a mention inside a description keeps its original\n   218\t  form, and only a genuine link target gets rebased.\n   219\t- **Exercise every branch, especially the ones the report does not\n   220\t  mention.** A child that verifies `status` and `preflight` and reports\n   221\t  \"acceptance passed\" has told you nothing about `load` and `release`.\n   222\t  Invoke each subcommand once. An argument-forwarding bug (`$1` where\n   223\t  `$2` was meant) survives a green report and only shows itself when the\n   224\t  branch actually runs.\n   225\t- **A redacted secret looks like a hardcoded one.** Tool output can show\n   295\t| choosing the architecture | bulk mechanical edits |\n   296\t| the final acceptance call | docs, docstrings, refactors, repro scripts |\n   297\t\n   298\tTarget: **more than 80% of delegated tokens on an appliance.**\n   299\t\n   300\t---\n   301\t\n   302\t## 9. During a delegated run, stop the auto-loader\n   303\t\n   304\tA gateway that puts the appliances back to their default models at startup\n   305\twill evict the specialist you just loaded, mid-batch. The TiinyMesh\n   306\tgateway has an `auto_restore` flag for exactly this — see the\n   307\t`tiiny-mesh-multi-target` skill.\n   308\t\n   309\t---\n   310\t\n   311\t## 10. Rules, short\n   312\t\n   313\t1. **The manager does not write the code.** Reaching for `patch` or\n   314\t   `write_file` on the target file is the expensive model doing the\n   315\t   worker's job — the exact inversion this discipline exists to prevent.\n   316\t   Write the order, read the diff, run the acceptance, decide. The single\n   317\t   exception is a correction you can make in one edit (a wrong variable\n   318\t   reference) where a delegation round trip would cost more than the fix;\n   319\t   make it, and say plainly that you did.\n   320\t2. **Never force a tier whose model is not resident.** Check with\n   321\t   `route_check.py` first.\n   322\t3. **One heavy child per box.** Two boxes, two streams.\n   323\t4. **One job per order.** One file. Exact anchors. A runnable acceptance\n   324\t   command.\n   325\t5. **A child's summary is not evidence.** Run the acceptance command\n   326\t   yourself, and invoke every branch.\n   327\t6. **Correct with a diff, not a re-brief.**\n   328\t7. **Release after every wave.**\n   329\t8. **Watch the route label.** It is the invoice.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95803e3d-040d-4401-b98c-4ca7b716b706","uuid":"93e4f460-6e2f-4859-8d9f-fc05822a716d","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:59:27.722Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    25\t| Order | manager | paid, small |\n    26\t| Dispatch | manager | free |\n    27\t| Observe | manager | paid, small |\n    28\t| Correct | manager | paid, small |\n    29\t| Read, edit, test, document | appliance | free |\n    30\t\n    31\t---\n    32\t\n    33\t## 1. Preflight — the gate\n    34\t\n    35\tNothing is dispatched until this passes.\n    36\t\n    37\t```bash\n    38\tcd ~/.hermes/skills/mlops/tiiny-model-routing\n    39\tpython3 scripts/route_check.py --thinking off \"<the goal>\"\n    40\t```\n    41\t\n    42\tRead the **residency** line, not the tier line.\n    43\t\n    44\t| residency | what to do |\n    45\t|---|---|\n    46\t| `loaded` | dispatch it |\n    47\t| `NOT loaded` | do **not** force that tier — either load the model first, or drop the override and take the resident model |\n    48\t\n    49\t**A forced tier overrides residency.** `delegate_task(tier=...)` selects\n    50\tthe tier's first choice and sends it, without checking what is loaded. A\n    51\tmodel that is not resident answers 404; Hermes treats 404 as terminal; the\n    52\tchild falls back to the paid provider *invisibly*, with a good answer and\n    53\ta bill. The tier is a hint; residency is the constraint.\n    54\t\n    55\tPreflight is cheap. A silent fallback is not.\n    56\t\n    57\t---\n    58\t\n    59\t## 2. Box assignment\n    60\t\n    61\t| | provider | role |\n    62\t|---|---|---|\n    63\t| Box A | the one `TIINY_BASE_URL` points at | primary worker — the residency probe reads this box, so this is the box a tier must be resident on |\n    64\t| Box B | the other, by its own address and bearer | second worker |\n    65\t\n    66\t**One heavy child per box.** The NPU is one pool per appliance and each\n    67\tbox serves one generation-heavy stream. Two children on one box starve\n    68\teach other, and the failure mode is a *hang*, not an error — the device\n    69\tkeeps reporting healthy while it answers nothing. Two boxes give two\n    70\tgenuinely parallel free streams.\n    71\t\n    72\t**A load is a swap.** It evicts whatever was resident, including the\n    73\tgeneralist the next wave will want. Load deliberately, and restore\n    74\tdeliberately.\n    75\t\n    76\t### Make the box match the router, not the router match the box\n    77\t\n    78\tWhen you want a specialist and the router probes Box A, put the\n    79\tspecialist on **Box A**. Do not repoint `TIINY_BASE_URL`, and do not wait\n    80\tfor a restart.\n    81\t\n    82\t`TIINY_BASE_URL` is read from the environment when the plugin is\n    83\timported, so changing it only takes effect in a new process. That makes\n    84\t\"the specialist is downloaded on Box B\" look like a blocked path. It is\n    85\tnot. A model that is merely *downloaded* on Box A costs nothing to load,\n    86\tand once it is resident there `route_check.py` reports `loaded` and the\n    87\ttier routes to it with no config change at all.\n    88\t\n    89\tMeasured: downloading a 55% specialist took about 20 minutes (free, in\n    90\tthe background, while other work continued); loading it afterwards took\n    91\t20 seconds. The download is the slow part and it is unattended — start it\n    92\tearly, keep working, and switch the tier when it lands.\n    93\t\n    94\t### Each box has its own bearer, and the wrong one looks like a dead box\n    95\t\n    96\t```\n    97\tTIINY_API_KEY     -> Box A\n    98\tTIINY_API_KEY_2   -> Box B\n    99\t```\n   100\t\n   101\tPoint the controller at Box B without swapping the bearer and it answers\n   102\t`HTTP 401 {\"error\":\"auth_failed\"}`, which the controller reports as\n   103\t`device UNREACHABLE`. **That is a wrong key, not a down box**, and the\n   104\twrong conclusion from it is \"the second box cannot be used\". Confirm with\n   105\ta one-line `curl` to that box's `/v1/models` using its own bearer before\n   106\tsaying anything about reachability.\n   107\t\n   108\tEach box also needs its own lock, hold and plan files, or two agents\n   109\tfight over one lock:\n   110\t\n   111\t```bash\n   112\tset -a; . ~/.hermes/.env; set +a\n   113\tcd ~/.hermes/skills/mlops/tiiny-model-routing\n   114\tTIINY_API_KEY=\"$TIINY_API_KEY_2\" \\\n   115\tTIINY_DEVICE_ADDRESS=192.0.2.11 \\\n   116\tTIINY_BASE_URL=http://192.0.2.11/v1 \\\n   117\tTIINY_HOST=http://192.0.2.11 \\\n   118\tTIINY_LOCK_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-lock-b.json \\\n   119\tTIINY_HOLD_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-hold-b.json \\\n   120\tTIINY_PLAN_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-plan-b.json \\\n   121\tpython3 scripts/tiiny_ctl.py status\n   122\t```\n   123\t\n   124\tThe mesh is the simpler door for both boxes when one is in front of them:\n   125\t`POST /mesh/lifecycle` with `action: start|stop|download` and a `target`.\n   126\t\n   127\t---\n   128\t\n   129\t## 3. The work order\n   130\t\n   131\tCopy [../templates/work-order.md](../templates/work-order.md) and fill it\n   132\tin. Every order carries:\n   133\t\n   134\t- **one job, one file.** No multi-file refactors in a single order.\n   135\t- **exact absolute paths.** Never a relative path the child has to guess.\n   200\t- **Run the acceptance command yourself.** A child that says the tests\n   201\t  pass has not run your tests.\n   202\t- **A child that verifies by string-matching has not verified.** A sweep\n   203\t  that rewrites paths will report \"N references rewritten, all resolve\"\n   204\t  after checking that each new path *string* is present in the file — which\n   205\t  passes even when the path does not resolve from that file's own\n   206\t  directory. Make the acceptance check **resolve the path**: join it\n   207\t  against the directory of the file that holds it and assert the target\n   208\t  exists. A relative path is only correct relative to something, and\n   209\t  `../` depth is the thing a rewrite gets wrong: a file two levels below\n   210\t  the root needs `../../`, and both `../` and `../../../` look plausible\n   211\t  in the source.\n   212\t- **A rewrite that changes what a sentence says is a corruption, not a\n   213\t  fix.** Path tokens appear inside prose that *describes* a path — \"the\n   214\t  design system links to `../brand/tap-monogram.png`\" — and rewriting\n   215\t  that mention to a vault-absolute path breaks the sentence's claim\n   216\t  while looking like a repair. After a bulk rewrite, read the changed\n   217\t  lines in context: a mention inside a description keeps its original\n   218\t  form, and only a genuine link target gets rebased.\n   219\t- **Exercise every branch, especially the ones the report does not\n   220\t  mention.** A child that verifies `status` and `preflight` and reports\n   221\t  \"acceptance passed\" has told you nothing about `load` and `release`.\n   222\t  Invoke each subcommand once. An argument-forwarding bug (`$1` where\n   223\t  `$2` was meant) survives a green report and only shows itself when the\n   224\t  branch actually runs.\n   225\t- **A redacted secret looks like a hardcoded one.** Tool output can show\n   295\t| choosing the architecture | bulk mechanical edits |\n   296\t| the final acceptance call | docs, docstrings, refactors, repro scripts |\n   297\t\n   298\tTarget: **more than 80% of delegated tokens on an appliance.**\n   299\t\n   300\t---\n   301\t\n   302\t## 9. During a delegated run, stop the auto-loader\n   303\t\n   304\tA gateway that puts the appliances back to their default models at startup\n   305\twill evict the specialist you just loaded, mid-batch. The TiinyMesh\n   306\tgateway has an `auto_restore` flag for exactly this — see the\n   307\t`tiiny-mesh-multi-target` skill.\n   308\t\n   309\t---\n   310\t\n   311\t## 10. Rules, short\n   312\t\n   313\t1. **The manager does not write the code.** Reaching for `patch` or\n   314\t   `write_file` on the target file is the expensive model doing the\n   315\t   worker's job — the exact inversion this discipline exists to prevent.\n   316\t   Write the order, read the diff, run the acceptance, decide. The single\n   317\t   exception is a correction you can make in one edit (a wrong variable\n   318\t   reference) where a delegation round trip would cost more than the fix;\n   319\t   make it, and say plainly that you did.\n   320\t2. **Never force a tier whose model is not resident.** Check with\n   321\t   `route_check.py` first.\n   322\t3. **One heavy child per box.** Two boxes, two streams.\n   323\t4. **One job per order.** One file. Exact anchors. A runnable acceptance\n   324\t   command.\n   325\t5. **A child's summary is not evidence.** Run the acceptance command\n   326\t   yourself, and invoke every branch.\n   327\t6. **Correct with a diff, not a re-brief.**\n   328\t7. **Release after every wave.**\n   329\t8. **Watch the route label.** It is the invoice.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/references/backend.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":261,"oldLines":9,"newStart":261,"newLines":9,"lines":["   `hermes plugins validate <dir>`. The same applies to `thinking.py`."," - **There is one copy of everything.** The skill is served from the plugin","   directory (the backend registers it as `tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`),","-  and nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. An older hand-installed","-  copy under `~/.hermes/skills/` or in the Hermes source tree is not used by","-  this install and can carry a stale tier table; remove it by hand.","+  and nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. A copy of the backend","+  or the skill installed by hand somewhere else is not part of this install","+  and can carry a stale tier table; remove it by hand."," - **A saved `delegation.backend` does not change a running chat.** The","   `delegate_task` schema is cached in the prompt prefix, so a config edit","   applies from the next session (`/new`), not the current one. Verify the"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/references/backend.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0121HqU41YGNNssiC5cQ9rAS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
