{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFZautDV8FEKWnAiKto9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JPjwnfPvxZbhqLZBrhTTeC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='tiiny-router/references/lifecycle.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na='''When the controller finds one (the directory named by the `TIINY_VAULT`\nsetting, or a parent of the controller holding both `hot.md` and\n`skills/`), the lock is announced there in a marked block.'''\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,'''To have the lock announced there, set `TIINY_VAULT` (in the environment\nor `~/.hermes/.env`) to the directory that holds `hot.md`; the controller\nthen writes a marked block into it.''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tiiny-router/SKILL.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\ndef cut(start,end,new=''):\n    global s\n    i=s.index(start); j=s.index(end,i)\n    s=s[:i]+new+s[j:]\n\nrep('''`TIINY_API_KEY` (Hermes keeps it in `~/.hermes/.env`; the controller finds\n  it there, in the environment, or in the vault's credentials file).''','''`TIINY_API_KEY` (Hermes keeps it in `~/.hermes/.env`; the controller finds\n  it there or in the environment).''')\nrep('''- The routing backend plugin installed (see [references/backend.md](references/backend.md)), and\n  `delegation.backend: tiiny-router` set in the active profile's config.''','''- The plugin installed with `npx hermes-tiiny-router install` (see\n  [references/backend.md](references/backend.md)), and\n  `delegation.backend: tiiny-router` set in the active profile's config.\n  The installer offers to set it; `npx hermes-tiiny-router doctor` reports\n  whether the install and the config are complete.''')\nrep('''This skill ships inside the plugin directory and the backend registers''','''This skill ships inside the plugin directory\n  (`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`) and the backend registers''')\nrep('''| **The router** (`plugin/`) |''','''| **The router** (`__init__.py`, `tiers.py`, `thinking.py`) |''')\n# mesh section\ncut('## Pointing the router at the mesh','## Quick Reference')\nrep('''### The commands\n\n| Command |''','''### The commands\n\nPaths in this skill are relative to the installed directory,\n`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` (`HERMES_HOME` defaults to\n`~/.hermes`). From anywhere else, `npx hermes-tiiny-router ctl ...` runs\n`scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` and `npx hermes-tiiny-router route-check ...` runs\n`scripts/route_check.py`, with the same arguments.\n\n| Command |''')\nrep('''  --goal \"index every file under the vault and classify each\" \\\\''','''  --goal \"index every file in the notes folder and classify each\" \\\\''')\nrep('''This takes the lock and writes a notice into the vault's `hot.md` so other\nagents in the AMC can see that Tiiny is spoken for. If the device is already\nheld, the reserve **refuses** and tells you who holds it and until when.\n\n*Done when:* the lock is held and the notice is in `hot.md`.''','''This takes the lock and, when a shared `hot.md` board is configured (see\n[The lock](#the-lock)), writes a notice into it so other agents can see that\nTiiny is spoken for. If the device is already held, the reserve **refuses**\nand tells you who holds it and until when.\n\n*Done when:* the lock is held, and the notice is on the board if there is one.''')\nrep('''hold, clears the plan, releases the lock, and removes the notice from\n`hot.md`.''','''hold, clears the plan, releases the lock, and removes the notice from the\nboard.''')\nrep('''free, and `hot.md` no longer carries the notice.''','''free, and the board no longer carries the notice.''')\nrep('''model's figures changed, the tier table in `plugin/tiers.py` is now wrong —\nupdate it, and update\n[`tiiny-discovery/tiiny-model-catalogue.md`](../../Tiiny/model-catalogue.md)\nto match.''','''model's figures changed, the tier table in `tiers.py` is now wrong --\nupdate it in the package and reinstall (see\n[references/backend.md](references/backend.md#changing-a-tier)).''')\ncut('When you need a publication-ready catalogue','*Done when:* the diff is empty')\nrep('''*Done when:* the diff is empty, or the differences are reflected in the tier\ntable and the catalogue.''','''*Done when:* the diff is empty, or the differences are reflected in the tier\ntable.''')\nrep('''python3 scripts/route_check.py --thinking off \"index every file under the vault\"''','''python3 scripts/route_check.py --thinking off \"index every file in the notes folder\"''')\nrep('''| **The announcement** | A marked block in the vault's `hot.md` — the AMC's own board of what is in flight — so agents that are not Hermes profiles can see the device is spoken for. |''','''| **The announcement** | Optional. A marked block in a shared `hot.md` board of what is in flight, so agents that are not Hermes profiles can see the device is spoken for. Set `TIINY_VAULT` (environment or `~/.hermes/.env`) to the directory holding `hot.md`; with no board the announcement is skipped. |''')\nrep('''`status` shows both. `release` clears both.''','''`status` shows both. `release` clears both.''')\nrep('''not a model). A vault `AGENTS.md` that describes''','''not a model). An `AGENTS.md` that describes''')\n# mesh restore / traffic paragraphs\ncut('**The mesh gateway has a restore path, and it is inert by design.**','- **`ensure` replaces it.**')\nrep('''To disable, set the environment variable ``TIINY_ENSURE_ON_ROUTE=false`` or\nedit ``ENSURE_ON_ROUTE`` in the plugin.''','''To disable, set the environment variable `TIINY_ENSURE_ON_ROUTE=false`.''')\ncut('**One list, one file.**','**Trimming is a functional decision',\n'''**One list, one file.** `REQUIRED_MODELS` in `scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` is the\nonly copy, and the installed directory holds the only installed copy of the\ncontroller. Change the list in the package and run `install` again; an edit\nmade in the installed directory is a local edit, which `install` refuses to\noverwrite without `--force` and `doctor` reports.\n\n''')\nrep('''which serves it from its own process at no NPU cost. See\n`mlops/offgrid-local-inference`. The appliance's''','''which serves it from its own process at no NPU cost. The appliance's''')\ncut('''`references/required-set-drift.md` keeps the audit recipe''','## Scheduled work on the device')\ncut('### Do not route scheduled work through the mesh','### Look for the provider block before you write one')\nrep('''`providers:` usually already carries a block per box — `tiiny`, `tiiny2`,\n`tiinymesh` — each complete''','''`providers:` usually already carries a block per box (`tiiny`, `tiiny2`),\neach complete''')\nrep('''  Nothing on a timer unloads a model either — an eviction comes from another\n  load, which in practice means a mesh `policy` route pointing at the wrong\n  box. Read `policy` before a long run, not the clock.''','''  Nothing on a timer unloads a model either -- an eviction comes from another\n  load.''')\nrep('''them differently (16 models on one, 42 on the other). That is what makes\n  one box the pinned vault and the other the flex box.''','''them differently (16 models on one, 42 on the other). That is what makes\n  one box the pinned box and the other the flex box.''')\nrep('''  its own lock/hold/plan/snapshot files. For both boxes at once, use\n  `POST /mesh/lifecycle` `{action, model, target}` on the mesh gateway, or the\n  box's own `POST /api/v1/models/<id>/start|stop` with its bearer — both run\n  concurrently, no CLI session involved.''','''  its own lock/hold/plan/snapshot files. For both boxes at once, use each\n  box's own `POST /api/v1/models/<id>/start|stop` with its bearer; the two\n  run concurrently, with no CLI session involved.''')\nrep('''  fallback points to an active provider with working credits (e.g., OpenRouter).\n  The `/mesh/fallback` route on TiinyMesh flips both the mesh chat secondary and\n  Hermes's `delegation.fallback_providers` in lockstep between OpenRouter and MiniMax.''','''  fallback points to an active provider with working credits (e.g., OpenRouter).''')\nrep('''  against OpenRouter unless the system CA store / `certifi` bundle is loaded\n  (as in `mesh._ssl_context()`).''','''  against OpenRouter unless the system CA store / `certifi` bundle is loaded.''')\ncut('- **Absolute paths and vault-local prefixes are publish-blockers.**','- **This skill never downloads a model.**',\n'''- **The package is the source; the installed directory is a copy.** The\n  backend, the controller and this skill are installed together into\n  `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` by `npx hermes-tiiny-router install`.\n  A hand edit there is a local edit: `doctor` reports it, and the next\n  `install` stops rather than overwrite it unless given `--force`. Make\n  lasting changes in the package and install again.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n -i 'vault\\|mesh\\|plugin/\\|hot.md\\|sync\\|symlink\\|required-set-drift\\|\\.\\./' tiiny-router/SKILL.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1239,"cache_read_input_tokens":112394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1239},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95803e3d-040d-4401-b98c-4ca7b716b706","uuid":"89cf0787-2e68-4dfc-b918-056aa13a64de","timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:00:24.972Z","request_id":"req_011ChFZauiYik5jZSNrtD4Px","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JPjwnfPvxZbhqLZBrhTTeC":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='tiiny-router/references/lifecycle.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na='''When the controller finds one (the directory named by the `TIINY_VAULT`\nsett