4,"oldLines":7,"newStart":74,"newLines":7,"lines":[" path**, not by package name, for a specific reason: the Hermes plugin loader"," executes `__init__.py` through `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location`,"," which does not establish package semantics, so a relative","-`from .tiers import ...` fails there — and the scripts run outside Hermes","+`from .tiers import ...` fails there -- and the scripts run outside Hermes"," entirely, where `from agent...` is not importable at all. Loading the file"," by path works in both places."," "]},{"oldStart":118,"oldLines":7,"newStart":118,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ```"," "," A tier can hold several candidates. The first is the default; the rest are","-fallbacks, in the order the device's own model descriptions support — and the","+fallbacks, in the order the device's own model descriptions support -- and the"," router actually *uses* them, because it knows which models are resident. The"," next section is about that, and it is the part that makes the tier table more"," than a lookup table."]},{"oldStart":129,"oldLines":7,"newStart":129,"newLines":7,"lines":[" loaded\"`, Hermes classifies that as terminal, and the child falls back to the"," paid provider. On a device whose shared NPU pool holds a handful of models at"," a time, that turns a routing decision into a silent move off the local","-device — and the work still completes, so nothing looks wrong.","+device -- and the work still completes, so nothing looks wrong."," "," So the router reads the device's resident set and picks something that is"," actually there:"]},{"oldStart":179,"oldLines":7,"newStart":179,"newLines":7,"lines":[" else. Loading is still the operator's call, made with the swap script."," "," **Fail open.** If the device is unreachable, the key is missing, or the lookup","-times out, the router returns the tier's first choice — exactly the behaviour","+times out, the router returns the tier's first choice -- exactly the behaviour"," from before residency was considered. A routing decision is not a place to"," fail."," "]},{"oldStart":246,"oldLines":20,"newStart":246,"newLines":20,"lines":[" "," Four details are decisions rather than defaults:"," ","-**`raise DelegationRouteError`** — an unknown tier is refused, not mapped to","+**`raise DelegationRouteError`** -- an unknown tier is refused, not mapped to"," the fallback. The message becomes the `delegate_task` tool error the model"," reads, so it should read as an instruction. An unknown thinking mode is"," refused the same way."," ","-**`merge_request_overrides`** — the delegation section may already carry an","+**`merge_request_overrides`** -- the delegation section may already carry an"," `extra_body` of its own, and dropping it would silently change the request"," for every other key in it. `extra_body` is merged one level deep; the single"," values (`reasoning_effort`, `max_tokens`) are replaced wholesale, because a"," half-applied one is worse than either."," ","-**`label`** — a short string carried on the child's result, so the route can","+**`label`** -- a short string carried on the child's result, so the route can"," be read back after the fact. Without it, \"which model actually ran this?\" is","-unanswerable. When the router substituted a model, the label says so — and","+unanswerable. When the router substituted a model, the label says so -- and"," when it asked for a reasoning mode, the label says the state the model"," **reached**, which is not always the one that was asked for."," "]},{"oldStart":321,"oldLines":8,"newStart":321,"newLines":8,"lines":[" Two decisions in that are worth stating plainly."," "," **\"Off\" on a model with no switch means its cheapest level, not a refusal.**","-The model still reasons; it just reasons less. The alternative — refusing the","-task, or claiming reasoning stopped when it did not — is worse than doing the","+The model still reasons; it just reasons less. The alternative -- refusing the","+task, or claiming reasoning stopped when it did not -- is worse than doing the"," work at the cheapest setting."," "," **The device's `toggleable` flag is a hint, not ground truth.** A model"]},{"oldStart":338,"oldLines":7,"newStart":338,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," A reasoning model spends its budget on the trace first. With a small"," `max_tokens`, the trace eats the whole budget and the request comes back","-**HTTP 200 with an empty answer** — the same status code as a successful","+**HTTP 200 with an empty answer** -- the same status code as a successful"," call, with nothing in it."," "," So the route applies an output floor whenever a model's reasoning is in play,"]},{"oldStart":395,"oldLines":7,"newStart":395,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," The fallback matters: if the device is unreachable, the batch should still"," complete on a paid provider rather than fail. It should be visible when it","-happens — a silent fallback means the local tier is not actually being used.","+happens -- a silent fallback means the local tier is not actually being used."," "," ---"," "]},{"oldStart":501,"oldLines":14,"newStart":501,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," **A stale hold is the hazard.** One left behind stops the watchdog from ever"," restoring the device, so the script needs `--restore` and `--clear` to clear","-one — and it needs to *check* that it cleared it. A script that prints \"hold","+one -- and it needs to *check* that it cleared it. A script that prints \"hold"," cleared\" without verifying is exactly how a hold outlives the batch that"," created it."," "," Two changes remove the hazard rather than documenting it."," "," **The hold file is released by truncating it, not only by deleting it.**","-Truncation is a write, and a write works in every context — including a","+Truncation is a write, and a write works in every context -- including a"," sandbox that blocks deletion outright:"," "," ```bash"]},{"oldStart":522,"oldLines":7,"newStart":522,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **The watchdog honours a hold only while it still means something.** An empty"," hold file is a released hold. A hold older than a grace window is honoured","-only if its model is still resident — otherwise it protects nothing and the","+only if its model is still resident -- otherwise it protects nothing and the"," device is restored:"," "," ```bash"]},{"oldStart":551,"oldLines":7,"newStart":551,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ```"," "," The grace window covers the gap between writing the hold and finishing the","-load it exists to protect — the hold is written *before* the load, precisely","+load it exists to protect -- the hold is written *before* the load, precisely"," so the watchdog cannot fire in between."," "," One more portability note, because it will bite anyone running the script"]},{"oldStart":564,"oldLines":7,"newStart":564,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## 2b. The device controller"," "," The swap script is for a human at a terminal. A manager agent running a batch","-needs the same things done for it, in order, without a human in the loop — and","+needs the same things done for it, in order, without a human in the loop -- and"," it needs the device kept away from other agents while it works."," "," `scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` is that. Seven commands:"]},{"oldStart":588,"oldLines":7,"newStart":588,"newLines":7,"lines":[" actually runs on:"," "," ```","-controller: plan → reserve → load       |  plugin: route_task","+controller: plan -> reserve -> load     |  plugin: route_task"," controller: release                     |  child runs on the plan's model"," ```"," "]},{"oldStart":609,"oldLines":7,"newStart":609,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," - the wave's own models are sacred;"," - of everything else resident, the cheapest are kept while they fit in what","-  is left — a 5% TTS model is worth keeping, a 47% generalist is not, when a","+  is left -- a 5% TTS model is worth keeping, a 47% generalist is not, when a","   wave needs the pool;"," - everything dropped is restored by `release`."," "]},{"oldStart":625,"oldLines":14,"newStart":625,"newLines":14,"lines":[" shared status board, so agents that are not running this code can see the"," device is spoken for."," ","-Release is a *write*, not a delete — the released state goes into the file.","+Release is a *write*, not a delete -- the released state goes into the file."," Where deletion is blocked, that is the only way to release."," "," ### The catalogue refresh"," "," `catalog --refresh` diffs the live Model Store against the last snapshot and"," reports what is new, what is gone, and whose NPU share or context window","-moved. If a tier model's figures changed, the tier table is now wrong —","+moved. If a tier model's figures changed, the tier table is now wrong --"," update it. The snapshot records **facts**; the analysis around them is"," written by hand."," "]},{"oldStart":642,"oldLines":7,"newStart":642,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," `scripts/route_check.py` applies the same tier table and the same shape"," detection, then prints the tier, the model, the budget and what the model","-can do with reasoning — so a routing decision can be checked without","+can do with reasoning -- so a routing decision can be checked without"," spawning a child."," "," ```bash"]},{"oldStart":663,"oldLines":8,"newStart":663,"newLines":8,"lines":[" residency: loaded"," ```"," ","-The checker makes read-only calls — the device's resident model list, and the","-device's catalogue when a reasoning mode is asked for — and changes nothing","+The checker makes read-only calls -- the device's resident model list, and the","+device's catalogue when a reasoning mode is asked for -- and changes nothing"," on the device. The residency line comes from `tiiny top`."," "," It finds the plugin's shared modules relative to its own file, so the"]},{"oldStart":697,"oldLines":7,"newStart":697,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - [ ] A batch with mixed subtasks shows more than one model in its results."," - [ ] After a deliberate swap, the required models are resident again."," - [ ] **A plugin change is loaded, not just written.** Editing the plugin","-      file on disk changes nothing in a running gateway — Python has already","+      file on disk changes nothing in a running gateway -- Python has already","       imported the module. Reload it, and reload it *for every profile that","       runs it*, because a profile's delegation backend is resolved under that","       profile's home."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/docs/PATTERN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3,"newLines":7,"lines":[" A **routing layer that answers one question per delegated subtask: which"," model does this one get?** It sits above the delegation mechanism, inspects"," each task, and returns a model for that task alone. Nothing about it is","-Tiiny-specific except the numbers in the table below — the mechanism is a","+Tiiny-specific except the numbers in the table below -- the mechanism is a"," standard per-task routing hook, and the same shape works against any"," provider with a model library."," "]},{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":7,"newStart":17,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Task shape is what predicts which model does well. A goal that says \"index"," the notes folder\" is an indexing job regardless of what else it mentions. A research","-task *about* code is still a research task — keyword matching gets that one","+task *about* code is still a research task -- keyword matching gets that one"," wrong, because it finds \"code\" in the goal and routes to the coder."," "," Shape is not a keyword list either. It is the *operation* the task performs:"]},{"oldStart":56,"oldLines":7,"newStart":56,"newLines":7,"lines":[" This separation is load-bearing. A load is a swap: it evicts whatever was"," resident. If a routing decision could trigger a load, then a batch that"," spawned several children could evict the model out from under a sibling","-child that was already running — and the failing sibling would report a 404,","+child that was already running -- and the failing sibling would report a 404,"," which reads as a bad model id and sends the operator hunting in the wrong"," place."," "]},{"oldStart":73,"oldLines":7,"newStart":73,"newLines":7,"lines":[" The override must **fail loudly**. An unrecognised tier is refused outright,"," not silently mapped to the generalist. A typo in a routing parameter that"," quietly degrades every task to the fallback is worse than a typo that stops","-the batch — the first is invisible in the output and expensive in the","+the batch -- the first is invisible in the output and expensive in the"," tokens; the second is a failed run."," "," The case where this matters is the goal that understates the work. \"Read"]},{"oldStart":88,"oldLines":7,"newStart":88,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," 1. **The model is resident.** `tiiny top` is the ground truth. `tiiny ls`","    lists the whole store, and its NPU column shows a model's *size*, not","-   its load state — a model can be listed there and not loaded.","+   its load state -- a model can be listed there and not loaded."," 2. **The models the batch needs fit.** Their NPU shares must sum to 100% or","    less."," 3. **The route is the one intended.** The checker prints the tier, the"]},{"oldStart":115,"oldLines":7,"newStart":115,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ### The swap that evicts a sibling"," ","-A load is a swap. Loading a model evicts whatever was resident — verified on","+A load is a swap. Loading a model evicts whatever was resident -- verified on"," a device where loading `Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B` evicted the resident"," `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B`."," "]},{"oldStart":125,"oldLines":7,"newStart":125,"newLines":7,"lines":[" change that the batch itself caused."," "," The preventive measure is the separation above: the router chooses, and a","-separate controller loads — under a lock, with the batch's fit checked before","+separate controller loads -- under a lock, with the batch's fit checked before"," anything moves. The reactive measure is to restore the required set when the"," batch finishes, so the next batch does not inherit a device nobody"," configured."]},{"oldStart":167,"oldLines":7,"newStart":167,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ### The watchdog evicting a deliberate swap"," "," A device that reloads its required models on a timer will evict a model that","-was loaded deliberately for a long task — a research sweep running for twenty","+was loaded deliberately for a long task -- a research sweep running for twenty"," minutes, evicted at the four-minute mark by a reload that had no idea what"," was happening."," "]},{"oldStart":178,"oldLines":7,"newStart":178,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," The ordering detail is the whole bug. The hold check must run *before* the"," cold-check. Placed after it, a held device still reports as cold, the reload","-fires, and the deliberate swap is evicted — with the hold file sitting right","+fires, and the deliberate swap is evicted -- with the hold file sitting right"," there saying otherwise."," "," ### The goal that understates the work"]},{"oldStart":188,"oldLines":7,"newStart":188,"newLines":7,"lines":[" \"Read these logs and tell me what went wrong\" describes reading; the work is"," summarising."," ","-There is no signal in the text that fixes this — which is exactly why the","+There is no signal in the text that fixes this -- which is exactly why the"," override exists. The cost of the mistake is asymmetric: a drafting task sent"," to the generalist wastes some quality; a research task sent to the coder"," wastes the whole run."]},{"oldStart":198,"oldLines":7,"newStart":198,"newLines":7,"lines":[" Every model has a context ceiling, and the specialist chosen for a task's"," shape is not automatically the one with the largest window. Routing a task"," that needs a very large context to a model with a smaller window produces a","-truncated result rather than an error — the child returns something plausible","+truncated result rather than an error -- the child returns something plausible"," that is missing the beginning or the end."," "," This is the failure that looks like a model that suddenly got worse. The"]},{"oldStart":222,"oldLines":7,"newStart":222,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Hard refactoring, recovery from failed runs | `Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next` | 94% | 131072 |"," "," Read on 2026-11-09, when the store held 92 models. The shares have already","-moved once — a model that took 55% of the pool took 47% on this read — so","+moved once -- a model that took 55% of the pool took 47% on this read -- so"," re-read them before trusting this table."," "," Combinations that cannot be resident together, from the same read:"]},{"oldStart":240,"oldLines":7,"newStart":240,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Reasoning mode is part of the route"," "," Which model gets the task is only half the decision. The other half is","-whether that model reasons before it answers — and the answer is not the same","+whether that model reasons before it answers -- and the answer is not the same"," for every model in the table, which is why it cannot be a boolean in the"," config."," "]},{"oldStart":273,"oldLines":19,"newStart":273,"newLines":19,"lines":[" Before trusting a routing setup:"," "," - [ ] The tier table carries the NPU share and context window for every","-      model, read from the device — not from memory, and not from a","+      model, read from the device -- not from memory, and not from a","       previous read of the same table."," - [ ] Every model in the table exists in the device's store."," - [ ] The NPU shares of the models a batch needs sum to 100% or less, and a","       batch that does not fit is split into waves."," - [ ] The router chooses; a separate controller loads. The plugin never loads","       or unloads a model.","-- [ ] The controller decides what to evict before it loads — the device's own","+- [ ] The controller decides what to evict before it loads -- the device's own","       eviction choice is not batch-aware."," - [ ] The device is locked for the duration, and the lock expires."," - [ ] An unrecognised tier is refused, not silently mapped to the fallback."," - [ ] The generalist fallback is a deliberate choice, not an accident.","-- [ ] Reasoning mode is a per-task parameter — 'off' for mechanical work,","+- [ ] Reasoning mode is a per-task parameter -- 'off' for mechanical work,","       'on' for novel reasoning, 'auto' for the model's native behaviour."," - [ ] The control that is applied matches what the model honours, and the","       route reports the state the model actually reached."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/docs/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," An agency running agent fleets has a routing problem before it has a cost"," problem. The research sweep, the document index, the code fix, the browser","-run, and the summary all end up on the same model — because that is what a","+run, and the summary all end up on the same model -- because that is what a"," single pin does. Every subtask pays for one model's context window, whether"," or not it needs that window, and the specialist that would have done one of"," them better never gets a turn."]},{"oldStart":45,"oldLines":7,"newStart":45,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **NPU is one shared pool.** Every model carries an NPU share, and models whose"," shares sum above 100% cannot be resident at the same time. A load is a","-**swap**, not an add — it evicts whatever was resident.","+**swap**, not an add -- it evicts whatever was resident."," "," This is the number to check before anything else, and it is why \"which model"," is best\" is the wrong first question. The right first question is **\"what"]},{"oldStart":72,"oldLines":7,"newStart":72,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Routing by task shape"," "," The fix is to route each subtask to the model that matches its shape. Shape,","-not keyword — because shape is what predicts which model does well. A goal","+not keyword -- because shape is what predicts which model does well. A goal"," that mentions \"index the notes folder\" is an indexing job. A research task *about*"," code is still a research task, and keyword matching gets it wrong."," "]},{"oldStart":82,"oldLines":7,"newStart":82,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," | Task shape | Model | Why this one | NPU | Context |"," |---|---|---|---|---|","-| Long-running research | `InternScience/Sage-A1.5-Turbo` | Built for long, multi-step scientific and analytical tasks — literature investigation, evidence gathering — and it splits a task across parallel subagents and checks its own progress mid-task | 48% | 262144 |","+| Long-running research | `InternScience/Sage-A1.5-Turbo` | Built for long, multi-step scientific and analytical tasks -- literature investigation, evidence gathering -- and it splits a task across parallel subagents and checks its own progress mid-task | 48% | 262144 |"," | Bulk indexing, classification | `openai/gpt-oss-20b` | A mixture-of-experts model with only 3.6B parameters active per token out of 21B total, which keeps it fast and resource-light on-device | 27% | 131072 |"," | Terminal coding, repo navigation | `ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-Turbo` | A mixture-of-experts model activating about 3B of 35B parameters per token, built for repository-scale coding and agentic work | 54% | 262144 |"," | Repository-scale coding | `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` | A multimodal agentic coding model for repository-level reasoning, tool calling, and multi-step code execution; a sparse MoE activating only 3B of 35B parameters per token | 47% | 262144 |"]},{"oldStart":97,"oldLines":14,"newStart":97,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," A tier can also list a second and third choice, tried in order when the first"," is not resident. The coding tier's own first choice is","-`Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-Turbo` at 55% — and at 55% it cannot share","+`Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-Turbo` at 55% -- and at 55% it cannot share"," the pool with the 47% model, which is exactly why the fallback list exists."," "," ## Implementing the router"," "," A routing layer needs to answer one question per subtask: *which model does"," this one get?* In Hermes, that question is answered by a **delegation","-backend** — a plugin that implements `route_task`, called once per task with","+backend** -- a plugin that implements `route_task`, called once per task with"," that task's goal and context."," "," ```python"]},{"oldStart":147,"oldLines":14,"newStart":147,"newLines":14,"lines":[" decision rather than a default."," "," **The `general` fallback is deliberate.** A task whose shape is not","-recognised goes to `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` — the model that is good at","+recognised goes to `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` -- the model that is good at"," everything in the catalogue and mediocre at each. Being wrong about a"," specialist costs more than being mediocre at a general task."," "," **The router chooses; a separate controller loads.** The backend picks the"," model for a subtask and never touches the device. A load is a swap that"," evicts whatever was resident, so a routing decision made inside a delegation","-batch must not be able to yank a model out from under a sibling task — and","+batch must not be able to yank a model out from under a sibling task -- and"," the delegation plugin has no hook that says \"the batch is finished\"."," "," So the loading half is a separate command that the manager agent drives"]},{"oldStart":173,"oldLines":14,"newStart":173,"newLines":14,"lines":[" Hermes treats that as terminal, and the child falls back to the paid"," provider. On a device whose shared NPU pool holds a handful of models at a"," time, routing to a specialist that is not loaded silently moves the work off","-the local device — and the work still completes, so nothing looks wrong.","+the local device -- and the work still completes, so nothing looks wrong."," "," So the router asks the device what is resident and picks something that is"," actually there: the tier's own first choice, then another candidate from the"," same tier, then the generalist. The label on the route records the"," substitution (`code->generalist`), so it is visible rather than invisible in"," a fallback. If the device cannot be reached at all, the router behaves","-exactly as it did before — the tier's first choice.","+exactly as it did before -- the tier's first choice."," "," This is what makes the fallback list in `TIER_CHOICES` worth having. Without"," it, the tier table is a lookup table; with it, the router is the thing that"]},{"oldStart":190,"oldLines":7,"newStart":190,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Inference from the goal is a heuristic, and heuristics need an escape hatch."," The backend exposes a `tier` parameter per task, validated against the tier","-list and **refused** if it is not one of them — a typo must fail loudly","+list and **refused** if it is not one of them -- a typo must fail loudly"," rather than silently falling back to the generalist."," "," The case where this matters: a task that reads \"read these logs and tell me"]},{"oldStart":201,"oldLines":7,"newStart":201,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Reasoning mode is a routing decision too"," "," A reasoning model answers in two parts: the trace, and the answer. The trace","-is not free, and on mechanical work it is not wanted — indexing a folder does","+is not free, and on mechanical work it is not wanted -- indexing a folder does"," not need a chain of thought, it needs the folder."," "," So the backend takes a second per-task parameter, `thinking`, with three"]},{"oldStart":212,"oldLines":9,"newStart":212,"newLines":9,"lines":[" The obvious implementation is a boolean. It is also the wrong one, because"," the models in a catalogue do not agree on how reasoning is controlled:"," ","-- Some models have a **switch** — `enable_thinking: false` in the chat","+- Some models have a **switch** -- `enable_thinking: false` in the chat","   template's keyword arguments stops the trace dead.","-- Some models have only **levels** — `low`, `medium`, `high` — and their","+- Some models have only **levels** -- `low`, `medium`, `high` -- and their","   switch is ignored outright. The level is read at the **top level of the","   request**, not inside the chat template; put it in the wrong place and it","   is silently discarded."]},{"oldStart":238,"oldLines":19,"newStart":238,"newLines":19,"lines":[" It comes from `GET /v1/models` for a resident model and"," `GET /api/v1/models/online_models` for the whole store. A hand-maintained"," capability table would be simpler and would be wrong within one TiinyOS","-update — the Model Store changes, and a stale row is believed.","+update -- the Model Store changes, and a stale row is believed."," "," ### \"Off\" means the cheapest available state"," "," For a model with no working switch, `thinking: \"off\"` is **not a refusal and"," not a pretence**. It means the cheapest state the model offers: the lowest","-reasoning level it declares. The model still reasons — it just reasons less.","+reasoning level it declares. The model still reasons -- it just reasons less."," The routing table's own indexing model is one of these, so this is the case"," that matters in practice."," "," ### The label reports what happened"," ","-The route carries a label, and the label carries the achieved state — never","+The route carries a label, and the label carries the achieved state -- never"," the requested one:"," "," | Label | Meaning |"]},{"oldStart":269,"oldLines":7,"newStart":269,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," A reasoning model spends its budget on the trace first. With a small"," `max_tokens`, the trace eats the whole budget and the request comes back","-**HTTP 200 with an empty answer** — the same status code as a successful","+**HTTP 200 with an empty answer** -- the same status code as a successful"," call, with nothing in it. The router therefore applies an output floor"," whenever a model's reasoning is in play, including in the \"off\" state, where"," a model whose switch does not work still produces a trace."]},{"oldStart":280,"oldLines":11,"newStart":280,"newLines":11,"lines":[" is where most routing implementations break."," "," **A load is a swap.** Loading a model evicts the resident one. The evicted","-model's inference endpoint then returns `404` — which means *not resident*,","+model's inference endpoint then returns `404` -- which means *not resident*,"," not a bad model id. Read `/v1/models` to see what is actually loaded; it"," lists resident models, not the whole store."," ","-**The device decides what to evict — unless you decide first.** When a load","+**The device decides what to evict -- unless you decide first.** When a load"," does not fit, the device makes room by evicting something, and it does not"," know what the batch needs. Left to itself it kept the 47% generalist and"," evicted the 27% model the batch had just asked for, so the wave's own model"]},{"oldStart":307,"oldLines":7,"newStart":307,"newLines":7,"lines":[" **The watchdog fights you.** A device that reloads its required models every"," few minutes will evict the research model you just loaded for a long task,"," mid-task. The fix is a hold file: while it exists, the watchdog reloads","-nothing. The hold check has to run *before* the cold-check — put it after,","+nothing. The hold check has to run *before* the cold-check -- put it after,"," and a hold reads as \"cold\" and the reload evicts your model anyway."," "," **Restore what you displaced.** A delegated batch that swapped in a"]},{"oldStart":341,"oldLines":7,"newStart":341,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ### The image bonus"," "," The same device runs the image models, and the same controller picks the","-right one for the job — a text-accurate default for a logo, a","+right one for the job -- a text-accurate default for a logo, a"," high-fidelity model for detail that IS the subject, a character sheet for a"," turnaround, an adapter for cutting a subject out of an existing photo. It"," is the kind of thing that looks like a bonus and turns out to be the reason"]},{"oldStart":377,"oldLines":8,"newStart":377,"newLines":8,"lines":[" sent:    enable_thinking=false, reasoning_effort=low, max_tokens=4096"," ```"," ","-The checker reads the device's resident set — one read-only call to the local","-CLI — and the device's own capability for the model it picked. It changes","+The checker reads the device's resident set -- one read-only call to the local","+CLI -- and the device's own capability for the model it picked. It changes"," nothing on the device. It exists so a routing decision can be checked"," *before* a batch spends tokens on it."," "]},{"oldStart":387,"oldLines":7,"newStart":387,"newLines":7,"lines":[" **The routing table is device-specific.** The tier choices, NPU shares, and"," context windows here were read from one device's catalogue endpoint on"," 2026-11-09, when the store held 92 models. The store changes with every","-TiinyOS update, and the NPU shares have already moved once — a model that","+TiinyOS update, and the NPU shares have already moved once -- a model that"," took 55% of the pool took 47% on the read behind this article. **Re-read the"," numbers before trusting them.**"," "]},{"oldStart":412,"oldLines":9,"newStart":412,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," ## Where to go next"," ","-- [PATTERN.md](./PATTERN.md) — the routing pattern in full: the failure","+- [PATTERN.md](./PATTERN.md) -- the routing pattern in full: the failure","   modes, the tier design, and the reference checklist.","-- [IMPLEMENTATION.md](./IMPLEMENTATION.md) — the backend plugin, the swap","+- [IMPLEMENTATION.md](./IMPLEMENTATION.md) -- the backend plugin, the swap","   script, and an end-to-end setup checklist."," - [route_check.py](../tiiny-router/scripts/route_check.py) -- the routing","   checker. Once installed, run it as `npx hermes-tiiny-router route-check`."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/references/backend.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":7,"newStart":13,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **It chooses; it never loads.** The device's resident set is a shared, finite"," resource and a load is a swap that evicts whatever was resident, so the","-loading half of the job lives in `scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` — a step the manager","+loading half of the job lives in `scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` -- a step the manager"," agent takes explicitly. See [lifecycle.md](lifecycle.md)."," "," The two halves meet at the **plan** (`~/.hermes/tiiny-plan.json`): the"]},{"oldStart":77,"oldLines":7,"newStart":77,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ","    The fallback matters: if the device is unreachable, the batch should still","    complete on a paid provider rather than fail. It should also be visible","-   when it happens — a silent fallback means the local tier is not actually","+   when it happens -- a silent fallback means the local tier is not actually","    being used."," "," 4. Restart the agent so the plugin and the new schema are picked up. If the"]},{"oldStart":112,"oldLines":7,"newStart":112,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hold and the plan."," "," To confirm the backend is live, delegate a batch with mixed subtasks and read","-the `route` on each child's result — it carries the backend name and the","+the `route` on each child's result -- it carries the backend name and the"," tier label, with the achieved reasoning state on it."," "," ## Thinking mode"]},{"oldStart":178,"oldLines":7,"newStart":178,"newLines":7,"lines":[" plugin, the controller and the checker all read that one file, so they cannot"," drift apart. It is loaded by path rather than by package name, because the"," Hermes plugin loader executes `__init__.py` through `spec_from_file_location`","-— which does not establish package semantics, so a relative import would","+-- which does not establish package semantics, so a relative import would"," fail there. `thinking.py` is loaded the same way, and is kept free of"," Hermes imports so the standalone checker can use it too."," "]},{"oldStart":186,"oldLines":12,"newStart":186,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," Three edits, in this order, all in `tiers.py`:"," ","-1. `TIER_CHOICES` — the model id, its NPU share, and its context window. All","+1. `TIER_CHOICES` -- the model id, its NPU share, and its context window. All","    three come from the device; `tiiny_ctl.py catalog --refresh` tells you","    when they have moved.","-2. `TIER_MODEL` — derived from `TIER_CHOICES`; it needs no separate edit","+2. `TIER_MODEL` -- derived from `TIER_CHOICES`; it needs no separate edit","    unless a tier's default changes.","-3. `SHAPE_SIGNALS` — the signals that route a task to that tier. More","+3. `SHAPE_SIGNALS` -- the signals that route a task to that tier. More","    specific shapes come first; the first tier with a matching signal wins."," "," Make the change in the package, not in the installed directory: `install`"]},{"oldStart":202,"oldLines":12,"newStart":202,"newLines":12,"lines":[" ## Things that will bite"," "," - **The route's shape is the credential path.** The backend returns the","-  delegation section's own shape with only the model overridden — the way","+  delegation section's own shape with only the model overridden -- the way","   the default backend returns `dict(config)`. This is not cosmetic. A route","   with `base_url` set and `api_key` empty is a *direct endpoint*, and an","   empty key means **inherit the parent's key**. The parent runs on the paid","   provider, so the device would receive the wrong bearer and answer","-  `401 auth_failed` — and the child would fall back to the paid provider,","+  `401 auth_failed` -- and the child would fall back to the paid provider,","   invisibly. Returning the section's shape puts this backend on the","   provider-resolution branch, where the device's `key_env` is honoured."," - **The router reads residency, and that changes the route.** It queries"]},{"oldStart":215,"oldLines":18,"newStart":215,"newLines":18,"lines":["   model that is actually loaded: the plan's assignment if there is one, then","   the tier's first choice, then another candidate from the same tier, then","   the generalist. A model that is not resident answers `404 \"is not loaded\"`,","-  which Hermes treats as terminal and falls back to the paid provider — so","+  which Hermes treats as terminal and falls back to the paid provider -- so","   routing to an unloaded model silently moves work off the device. The","   route's `label` records any substitution (`code->generalist`). If the","   lookup fails, the router fails open to the tier's first choice."," - **The router never loads a model.** A load is a swap, and it evicts","-  whatever was resident — including the model a sibling task is using. The","+  whatever was resident -- including the model a sibling task is using. The","   controller does the loading, explicitly, under a lock."," - **An unknown tier is refused.** The override fails loudly rather than","   falling back to the generalist, because a silent fallback is invisible in","   the output and expensive in the tokens."," - **The task schema is cached.** `task_parameters()` and `description()` must","-  be deterministic for a given config — the schema is part of the cached","+  be deterministic for a given config -- the schema is part of the cached","   prompt prefix, so a non-deterministic result changes the prompt between","   calls."," - **Thinking mode is per task, not per config.** `thinking: \"auto\" | \"on\" |"]},{"oldStart":238,"oldLines":7,"newStart":238,"newLines":7,"lines":["   `enable_thinking` belongs in `extra_body.chat_template_kwargs`; a named","   level belongs at the **top level of the request**, not inside","   `chat_template_kwargs`. The same level name inside the chat template is a","-  different knob that some model families read and others ignore silently —","+  different knob that some model families read and others ignore silently --","   which looks configured and changes nothing."," - **The device's `toggleable` flag has been wrong.** A model flagged as","   having no on/off switch honours it anyway. Send the boolean whenever it"]},{"oldStart":252,"oldLines":11,"newStart":252,"newLines":11,"lines":["   fails open on every call."," - **A partially-installed plugin fails at load, not at use.** The plugin","   loader executes `__init__.py` through `spec_from_file_location`, so","-  `__init__.py` cannot use a relative import to reach `tiers.py` — it loads","+  `__init__.py` cannot use a relative import to reach `tiers.py` -- it loads","   that file by path. `install` copies the whole directory; a hand copy of","   just `__init__.py` and `plugin.yaml` is not enough. A tree with `__init__.py` but no","   `tiers.py` raises `ImportError` at load, and the backend is then simply","-  absent from `hermes plugins list` — which reads as \"never installed\"","+  absent from `hermes plugins list` -- which reads as \"never installed\"","   rather than \"installed wrong\". Validate with","   `hermes plugins validate <dir>`. The same applies to `thinking.py`."," - **There is one copy of everything.** The skill is served from the plugin"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/references/coding-delegation.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":7,"newStart":6,"newLines":7,"lines":[" costs nothing."," "," A 30B model on an appliance is not a frontier model. The difference is not","-capability — it is **briefing**. Give it a tight, verifiable order and it","+capability -- it is **briefing**. Give it a tight, verifiable order and it"," competes. Give it a vague one and it wanders, and the manager pays for"," the wandering twice: once in the box's tokens, once in a re-dispatch."," "]},{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":7,"newStart":30,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ---"," ","-## 1. Preflight — the gate","+## 1. Preflight -- the gate"," "," Nothing is dispatched until this passes."," "]},{"oldStart":43,"oldLines":7,"newStart":43,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | residency | what to do |"," |---|---|"," | `loaded` | dispatch it |","-| `NOT loaded` | do **not** force that tier — either load the model first, or drop the override and take the resident model |","+| `NOT loaded` | do **not** force that tier -- either load the model first, or drop the override and take the resident model |"," "," **A forced tier overrides residency.** `delegate_task(tier=...)` selects"," the tier's first choice and sends it, without checking what is loaded. A"]},{"oldStart":59,"oldLines":12,"newStart":59,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," | | provider | role |"," |---|---|---|","-| Box A | the one `TIINY_BASE_URL` points at | primary worker — the residency probe reads this box, so this is the box a tier must be resident on |","+| Box A | the one `TIINY_BASE_URL` points at | primary worker -- the residency probe reads this box, so this is the box a tier must be resident on |"," | Box B | the other, by its own address and bearer | second worker |"," "," **One heavy child per box.** The NPU is one pool per appliance and each"," box serves one generation-heavy stream. Two children on one box starve","-each other, and the failure mode is a *hang*, not an error — the device","+each other, and the failure mode is a *hang*, not an error -- the device"," keeps reporting healthy while it answers nothing. Two boxes give two"," genuinely parallel free streams."," "]},{"oldStart":87,"oldLines":7,"newStart":87,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Measured: downloading a 55% specialist took about 20 minutes (free, in"," the background, while other work continued); loading it afterwards took","-20 seconds. The download is the slow part and it is unattended — start it","+20 seconds. The download is the slow part and it is unattended -- start it"," early, keep working, and switch the tier when it lands."," "," ### Each box has its own bearer, and the wrong one looks like a dead box"]},{"oldStart":129,"oldLines":7,"newStart":129,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **one job, one file.** No multi-file refactors in a single order."," - **exact absolute paths.** Never a relative path the child has to guess."," - **exact anchors.** The function to change, the literal string to match","-  — quote it. \"Update the routing section\" is not an anchor.","+  -- quote it. \"Update the routing section\" is not an anchor."," - **a runnable acceptance command.** The child must make it pass, and the","   manager runs it again independently."," - **the output artifact path.**"]},{"oldStart":145,"oldLines":8,"newStart":145,"newLines":8,"lines":["   rebuild a **shipped** artifact: one that already went out, already carried","   hand-written content, and already had its own publication state recorded.","   The rebuild succeeds, reports clean, and silently replaces authored work","-  with a generated blank. Write the exclusion into the order — *\"edit ONLY","-  `<file>`; do not run the builder against `<live path>`\"* — and prefer a","+  with a generated blank. Write the exclusion into the order -- *\"edit ONLY","+  `<file>`; do not run the builder against `<live path>`\"* -- and prefer a","   builder that refuses to overwrite an existing output directory."," - **A generated placeholder is a trap when the output already has human","   content.** If the generator writes an empty marked placeholder (an analysis"]},{"oldStart":170,"oldLines":14,"newStart":170,"newLines":14,"lines":["   passing tests) in one shot."," "," Ask for raw findings on disk early and keep the summary short. That is","-what keeps a local model competitive with a frontier one — and it means a","+what keeps a local model competitive with a frontier one -- and it means a"," budget-exhausted child still leaves you its artifact rather than nothing."," "," **Tell it to write the file before it verifies it.** An appliance"," generates at roughly 20 tokens per second, so a 150-line script is minutes"," of pure generation. A child that composes perfectly and never writes"," loses everything if it stalls. A slightly imperfect file on disk that the","-manager can fix beats a perfect one that never lands — say so in the","+manager can fix beats a perfect one that never lands -- say so in the"," order itself."," "," That throughput is the real constraint on order size, not the model's"]},{"oldStart":196,"oldLines":7,"newStart":196,"newLines":7,"lines":["   pass has not run your tests."," - **A child that verifies by string-matching has not verified.** A sweep","   that rewrites paths will report \"N references rewritten, all resolve\"","-  after checking that each new path *string* is present in the file — which","+  after checking that each new path *string* is present in the file -- which","   passes even when the path does not resolve from that file's own","   directory. Make the acceptance check **resolve the path**: join it","   against the directory of the file that holds it and assert the target"]},{"oldStart":205,"oldLines":8,"newStart":205,"newLines":8,"lines":["   the root needs `../../`, and both `../` and `../../../` look plausible","   in the source."," - **A rewrite that changes what a sentence says is a corruption, not a","-  fix.** Path tokens appear inside prose that *describes* a path — \"the","-  design system links to `../brand/tap-monogram.png`\" — and rewriting","+  fix.** Path tokens appear inside prose that *describes* a path -- \"the","+  design system links to `../brand/tap-monogram.png`\" -- and rewriting","   that mention to an absolute path breaks the sentence's claim","   while looking like a repair. After a bulk rewrite, read the changed","   lines in context: a mention inside a description keeps its original"]},{"oldStart":219,"oldLines":24,"newStart":219,"newLines":24,"lines":["   branch actually runs."," - **A redacted secret looks like a hardcoded one.** Tool output can show","   `Bearer ***` where the file actually reads `Bearer $(_key)`. Check by","-  length, or grep for the literal value, before raising a leak alarm —","+  length, or grep for the literal value, before raising a leak alarm --","   that is the tool protecting the secret, not the child leaking it."," - Read the **route label**. `tiiny-router` means the box served it.","   Anything else means the paid provider did the work."," - If the child ran long, look for its file on disk before concluding it","-  produced nothing — the hang is often in the handover, not the work.","+  produced nothing -- the hang is often in the handover, not the work."," - **Record what you corrected, in the child's own report file.** When the","   child's work needed fixing, the report it left behind still claims the","   pre-fix state, so the next reader inherits a false record. Add the","   corrections to the report as a verification block naming each defect,","-  what it was, and how it was resolved — and state plainly whether the","+  what it was, and how it was resolved -- and state plainly whether the","   child's count and its self-check were accurate."," - **After a child runs a build, check what the build TOUCHED, not only what","   it was asked to change.** A child's report lists the files it meant to","   edit; it does not list the artifacts its build wrote. Compare the","   modification times of everything the build could have reached, or hash","   the shipped files before and after. A shipped file that changed without","-  appearing in the report was clobbered — and if it held authored content,","+  appearing in the report was clobbered -- and if it held authored content,","   the recovery path is whatever copy exists outside the tree (a scratch","   build directory, a version-control copy, the platform's own read-back),","   so **keep that copy before dispatching the child**."]},{"oldStart":273,"oldLines":9,"newStart":273,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," Three guards, strongest first:"," ","-1. **Preflight** — makes it nearly impossible.","-2. **The route label** — read it every wave.","-3. **A ledger** — count the children whose route is not `tiiny-router`.","+1. **Preflight** -- makes it nearly impossible.","+2. **The route label** -- read it every wave.","+3. **A ledger** -- count the children whose route is not `tiiny-router`.","    That count *is* the paid spend, and it should be zero."," "," ---"]},{"oldStart":306,"oldLines":7,"newStart":306,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," 1. **The manager does not write the code.** Reaching for `patch` or","    `write_file` on the target file is the expensive model doing the","-   worker's job — the exact inversion this discipline exists to prevent.","+   worker's job -- the exact inversion this discipline exists to prevent.","    Write the order, read the diff, run the acceptance, decide. The single","    exception is a correction you can make in one edit (a wrong variable","    reference) where a delegation round trip would cost more than the fix;"]}]}],"moreFiles":7,"changedFiles":["/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/docs/PATTERN.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/docs/README.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/SKILL.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/references/backend.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/references/coding-delegation.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/tiiny-router/references/imag