{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NK7ce5xxSeTowpHRCWo48P","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * The config step: select the routing backend in Hermes config. Config is\n * changed only through `hermes config set`; `config.yaml` and the secrets\n * file are never read or written here.\n */\nimport { readSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { isatty } from 'node:tty'\nimport { runHermes } from './hermes.js'\nimport { PLUGIN_NAME } from './package.js'\n\nexport type ConfigMode = 'configure'|'skip'|'ask'\n\n/** One `hermes config set KEY VALUE` call. */\nexport type ConfigSetting = [key:string, value:string]\n\n/**\n * Context window of each model in the `tiiny` provider. Mirrors the\n * provider block in `references/backend.md` and the tier table in\n * `tiers.py`; change them together.\n */\nconst TIINY_MODELS:Record<string, { context_length:number }> = {\n    'Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B': { context_length: 262144 },\n    'Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B': { context_length: 262144 },\n    'Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B': { context_length: 131072 },\n    'openai/gpt-oss-20b': { context_length: 131072 },\n    'ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-Turbo': { context_length: 262144 },\n    'InternScience/Sage-A1.5-Turbo': { context_length: 262144 },\n}\n\nconst PROVIDER = 'providers.tiiny'\n\n/**\n * Every setting the config step makes, in order. Model ids contain dots,\n * so the `models` map is set as one JSON value (valid YAML flow syntax)\n * rather than through dotted keys.\n */\nexport const SETTINGS:ConfigSetting[] = [\n    [`${PROVIDER}.name`, 'tiiny'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.api`, 'http://openai.api.tiiny/v1'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.key_env`, 'TIINY_API_KEY'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.transport`, 'chat_completions'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.default_model`, 'Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.context_length`, '262144'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.models_discovered`, 'false'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.extra_body.chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking`, 'false'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.models`, JSON.stringify(TIINY_MODELS)],\n    ['delegation.backend', PLUGIN_NAME],\n]\n\n/** Quote `s` for a POSIX shell. */\nfunction shellQuote (s:string):string {\n    if (/^[\\w./:@-]+$/.test(s)) return s\n    return `'${s.replaceAll(\"'\", `'\\\\''`)}'`\n}\n\n/** The settings as shell commands a user can run by hand. */\nexport function configCommands ():string[] {\n    return SETTINGS.map(([key, value]) =>\n        `hermes config set ${shellQuote(key)} ${shellQuote(value)}`)\n}\n25:    name:string;\n63:            name: 'installed directory',\n84:            name: 'version',\n98:            name: 'local edits',\n111:            name: 'hermes plugins validate',\n121:            name: 'delegation.backend',\n135:            name: 'python3',\n142:            name: 'device',\nsrc/install.ts:3: * write the manifest, then have Hermes validate it.\nsrc/install.ts:10:    buildManifest, compareManifest, listTree, readManifest, writeManifest,\nsrc/install.ts:15:    /** Overwrite local edits and directories this package did not write. */\nsrc/install.ts:26:function overwriteProblem (target:string):string|null {\nsrc/install.ts:42:    const problem = overwriteProblem(target)\nsrc/install.ts:47:                'Re-run with --force to overwrite.'\nsrc/install.ts:59:    writeManifest(target, buildManifest(target, files, packageVersion()))","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95803e3d-040d-4401-b98c-4ca7b716b706","uuid":"93a1f75d-c872-450a-b91b-88ffa9caa5a9","timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:02:04.339Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * The config step: select the routing backend in Hermes config. Config is\n * changed only through `hermes config set`; `config.yaml` and the secrets\n * file are never read or written here.\n */\nimport { readSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { isatty } from 'node:tty'\nimport { runHermes } from './hermes.js'\nimport { PLUGIN_NAME } from './package.js'\n\nexport type ConfigMode = 'configure'|'skip'|'ask'\n\n/** One `hermes config set KEY VALUE` call. */\nexport type ConfigSetting = [key:string, value:string]\n\n/**\n * Context window of each model in the `tiiny` provider. Mirrors the\n * provider block in `references/backend.md` and the tier table in\n * `tiers.py`; change them together.\n */\nconst TIINY_MODELS:Record<string, { context_length:number }> = {\n    'Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B': { context_length: 262144 },\n    'Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B': { context_length: 262144 },\n    'Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B': { context_length: 131072 },\n    'openai/gpt-oss-20b': { context_length: 131072 },\n    'ornith-ai/Ornith-1.5-35B-A3B-Turbo': { context_length: 262144 },\n    'InternScience/Sage-A1.5-Turbo': { context_length: 262144 },\n}\n\nconst PROVIDER = 'providers.tiiny'\n\n/**\n * Every setting the config step makes, in order. Model ids contain dots,\n * so the `models` map is set as one JSON value (valid YAML flow syntax)\n * rather than through dotted keys.\n */\nexport const SETTINGS:ConfigSetting[] = [\n    [`${PROVIDER}.name`, 'tiiny'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.api`, 'http://openai.api.tiiny/v1'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.key_env`, 'TIINY_API_KEY'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.transport`, 'chat_completions'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.default_model`, 'Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.context_length`, '262144'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.models_discovered`, 'false'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.extra_body.chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking`, 'false'],\n    [`${PROVIDER}.models`, JSON.stringify(TIINY_MODELS)],\n    ['delegation.backend', PLUGIN_NAME],\n]\n\n/** Quote `s` for a POSIX shell. */\nfunction shellQuote (s:string):string {\n    if (/^[\\w./:@-]+$/.test(s)) return s\n    return `'${s.replaceAll(\"'\", `'\\\\''`)}'`\n}\n\n/** The settings as shell commands a user can run by hand. */\nexport function configCommands ():string[] {\n    return SETTINGS.map(([key, value]) =>\n        `hermes config set ${shellQuote(key)} ${shellQuote(value)}`)\n}\n25:    name:string;\n63:            name: 'installed directory',\n84:            name: 'version',\n98:            name: 'local edits',\n111:            name: 'hermes plugins validate',\n121:            name: 'delegation.backend',\n135:            name: 'python3',\n142:            name: 'device',\nsrc/install.ts:3: * write the manifest, then have Hermes validate it.\nsrc/install.ts:10:    buildManifest, compareManifest, listTree, readManifest, writeManifest,\nsrc/install.ts:15:    /** Overwrite local edits and directories this package did not write. */\nsrc/install.ts:26:function overwriteProblem (target:string):string|null {\nsrc/install.ts:42:    const problem = overwriteProblem(target)\nsrc/install.ts:47:                'Re-run with --force to overwrite.'\nsrc/install.ts:59:    writeManifest(target, buildManifest(target, files, packageVersion()))","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NK7ce5xxSeTowpHRCWo48P","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFZkFm4KN6jtET8y4r7s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing the root README now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2383,"cache_read_input_tokens":138385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2383},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95803e3d-040d-4401-b98c-4ca7b716b706","uuid":"ad8a8e7c-b6dd-467c-b264-02165a932013","timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:02:05.441Z","request_id":"req_011ChFZkFWBBi5TrBKuCs9Pw"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFZkFm4KN6jtET8y4r7s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011aux7kesMpSZPxxuPArgDB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/README.md","content":"# hermes-tiiny-router\n\nTiiny model routing for the Hermes agent harness. When Hermes hands a\nsubtask to a subagent with `delegate_task`, the routing backend picks the\nTiiny model that fits that kind of work: indexing goes to `gpt-oss-20b`,\ncoding to `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B`, browser work to `Qwen3.8-27B`, and so on. The\npackage also ships the controller that loads models and locks the device,\nand a skill that teaches the manager agent the whole procedure.\n\nNeeds macOS or Linux, Node 20 or later, `python3`, the `hermes` CLI on\n`PATH`, and a Tiiny device on the LAN.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install\n```\n\nThis copies one directory to `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`\n(`HERMES_HOME` defaults to `~/.hermes`). It holds the routing backend, the\ncontroller scripts and the skill, which Hermes serves as\n`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`. The installer then runs\n`hermes plugins validate` on the directory.\n\nAdd the device's bearer to `~/.hermes/.env` yourself; the installer never\nreads or writes that file:\n\n```\nTIINY_API_KEY=...\n```\n\n## The config step\n\nAfter copying, `install` offers to select the backend in Hermes config. It\nchanges config only through `hermes config set`: it adds the `tiiny`\nprovider (endpoint, `key_env: TIINY_API_KEY`, the tier models and their\ncontext windows, reasoning off by default) and sets\n`delegation.backend` to `tiiny-router`.\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install                  # asks, when run in a terminal\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install --configure      # applies without asking\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install --no-configure   # skips the config step\n```\n\nWithout a terminal and without either flag, it skips the step and prints\nthe `hermes config set` commands so you can run them yourself.\n`delegation.fallback_providers` is not set; it depends on your paid\nprovider. See\n[tiiny-router/references/backend.md](tiiny-router/references/backend.md)\nfor the full provider block.\n\nA saved `delegation.backend` takes effect from the next Hermes session, not\nthe current one. Restart the gateway or start a new session.\n\n## Check the install\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router doctor\n```\n\n`doctor` prints a pass, warn or fail line for each check: the installed\ndirectory is complete, its version matches the package, no installed file\nwas edited, `hermes plugins validate` passes, `delegation.backend` selects\n`tiiny-router`, `python3` is present, and the device answers. It exits\nnon-zero when any check fails. A device that cannot be reached is a\nwarning, not a failure.\n\nTo see where a goal would be routed, and to drive the controller, run the\ninstalled scripts through the package:\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router route-check \"index every file in the notes folder\"\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router route-check --all\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router ctl status\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router ctl ensure --model \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\"\n```\n\n`route-check` and `ctl` run `scripts/route_check.py` and\n`scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` from the installed directory with the system\n`python3`, passing the arguments and the exit code through.\n\n## Upgrade\n\nRun `install` again with the newer package:\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router@latest install\n```\n\n`install` keeps a manifest of what it wrote. If a file in the installed\ndirectory was edited since then, or the directory was not installed by this\npackage (for example an older copy made by hand), it lists the problem and\nstops. Re-run with `--force` to overwrite.\n\n## Uninstall\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router uninstall\n```\n\nThis removes `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`, and only when its\nmanifest shows this package installed it. It does not change Hermes\nconfig; it prints the `hermes config set` command that unselects the\nbackend.\n\n## More\n\n- [tiiny-router/SKILL.md](tiiny-router/SKILL.md) -- the procedure the\n  manager agent follows: pick, fit, reserve, load, supervise, verify,\n  release.\n- [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) -- why routing by task shape pays off.\n- [docs/PATTERN.md](docs/PATTERN.md) -- the routing pattern in full.\n- [docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md](docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md) -- the backend, the\n  controller and an end-to-end checklist.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2383,"cache_read_input_tokens":138385,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2383},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95803e3d-040d-4401-b98c-4ca7b716b706","uuid":"cd06cdf2-8c8d-4e53-a029-7f1f60afce63","timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:02:18.278Z","request_id":"req_011ChFZkFWBBi5TrBKuCs9Pw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011aux7kesMpSZPxxuPArgDB":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-12-docs-for-package-install/README.md","content":"# hermes-tiiny-router\n\nTiiny model routing for the Hermes agent harness. When Hermes hands a\nsubtask to a subagent with `delegate_task`, the routing backend picks the\nTiiny model that fits that kind of work: indexing goes to `gpt-oss-20b`,\ncoding to `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B`, browser work to `Qwen3.8-27B`, and so on. The\npackage also ships the controller that loads models and locks the device,\nand a skill that teaches the manager agent the whole procedure.\n\nNeeds macOS or Linux, Node 20 or later, `python3`, the `hermes` CLI on\n`PATH`, and a Tiiny device on the LAN.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install\n```\n\nThis copies one directory to `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`\n(`HERMES_HOME` defaults to `~/.hermes`). It holds the routing backend, the\ncontroller scripts and the skill, which Hermes serves as\n`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`. The installer then runs\n`hermes plugins validate` on the directory.\n\nAdd the device's bearer to `~/.hermes/.env` yourself; the installer never\nreads or writes that file:\n\n```\nTIINY_API_KEY=...\n```\n\n## The config step\n\nAfter copying, `install` offers to select the backend in Hermes config. It\nchanges config only through `hermes config set`: it adds the `tiiny`\nprovider (endpoint, `key_env: TIINY_API_KEY`, the tier models and their\ncontext windows, reasoning off by default) and sets\n`delegation.backend` to `tiiny-router`.\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install                  # asks, when run in a terminal\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install --configure      # applies without asking\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router install --no-configure   # skips the config step\n```\n\nWithout a terminal and without either flag, it skips the step and prints\nthe `hermes config set` commands so you can run them yourself.\n`delegation.fallback_providers` is not set; it depends on your paid\nprovider. See\n[tiiny-router/references/backend.md](tiiny-router/references/backend.md)\nfor the full provider block.\n\nA saved `delegation.backend` takes effect from the next Hermes session, not\nthe current one. Restart the gateway or start a new session.\n\n## Check the install\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router doctor\n```\n\n`doctor` prints a pass, warn or fail line for each check: the installed\ndirectory is complete, its version matches the package, no installed file\nwas edited, `hermes plugins validate` passes, `delegation.backend` selects\n`tiiny-router`, `python3` is present, and the device answers. It exits\nnon-zero when any check fails. A device that cannot be reached is a\nwarning, not a failure.\n\nTo see where a goal would be routed, and to drive the controller, run the\ninstalled scripts through the package:\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router route-check \"index every file in the notes folder\"\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router route-check --all\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router ctl status\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router ctl ensure --model \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\"\n```\n\n`route-check` and `ctl` run `scripts/route_check.py` and\n`scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` from the installed directory with the system\n`python3`, passing the arguments and the exit code through.\n\n## Upgrade\n\nRun `install` again with the newer package:\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router@latest install\n```\n\n`install` keeps a manifest of what it wrote. If a file in the installed\ndirectory was edited since then, or the directory was not installed by this\npackage (for example an older copy made by hand), it lists the problem and\nstops. Re-run with `--force` to overwrite.\n\n## Uninstall\n\n```bash\nnpx hermes-tiiny-router uninstall\n```\n\nThis removes `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`, and only when its\nmanifest shows this package installed it. It does not change Hermes\nconfig; it prints the `hermes config set` command that unselects the\nbackend.\n\n## More\n\n- [tiiny-router/SKILL.md](tiiny-router/SKILL.md) -- the procedure the\n  manager agent follows: pick, fit, reserve, load, supervise, verify,\n  release.\n- [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) -- why routing by task shape pays off.\n- [docs/PATTERN.md](docs/PATTERN.md) -- the routing pattern in full.\n- [docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md](docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md) -- the backend, the\n  controller and an end-to-end checklist.\n"}}}
