{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D9xx2STd6pw1VTysnVocrT","type":"tool_result","content":"13:# Tiiny Model Routing\n26:## When to Use\n52:## Prerequisites\n80:## The two halves\n98:## The lifecycle\n117:## Quick Reference\n119:### The tiers\n139:### The commands\n160:## Picking a model for a project role\n176:## Procedure\n178:### 1 -- Evaluate the job\n191:### 2 -- Pick the model, and check it can run\n206:### 3 -- Ensure the combination fits\n218:### 4 -- Reserve the device\n231:### 5 -- Load the batch's models\n245:### 6 -- Plan the work: the device is single-threaded\n274:### 7 -- Supervise the child\n289:### 8 -- Check the child's work\n298:### 9 -- Release the device\n315:### 10 -- Keep the catalogue honest\n334:## Thinking mode\n352:### The device knows more than a table does\n380:### \"Off\" means the cheapest available state\n387:### The label reports what happened, not what was asked\n404:### Thinking on needs a token floor\n423:## The image benefit\n448:## The lock\n468:## The required set\n544:## Scheduled work on the device\n552:### Pin a job to the box\n568:### The pin is what makes the saving real\n576:### Look for the provider block before you write one\n584:### Contention is decided by agent windows, not by the clock\n593:### The cron inactivity watchdog\n606:## Pitfalls\n909:## Delegating coding work\n915:### Two rules from the author that decide whether you delegate at all\n973:## Verification\n- **The package is the source; the installed directory is a copy.** The\n  backend, the controller and this skill are installed together into\n  `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` by `npx hermes-tiiny-router install`.\n  A hand edit there is a local edit: `doctor` reports it, and the next\n  `install` stops rather than overwrite it unless given `--force`. Make\n  lasting changes in the package and install again.\n- **This skill never downloads a model.** It chooses and loads from what is\n  already on the device.\n\n## Delegating coding work\n\nThe discipline for making the appliance do the writing and the manager\nagent do the judging. The full method is in\n[references/coding-delegation.md](references/coding-delegation.md).\n\n### Two rules from the author that decide whether you delegate at all\n\n**A multi-part job delegates; it does not get done inline.** When a task has\nseveral parts -- a sweep, a rewrite, a build, a set of independent edits -- hand\nthe mechanical parts to a sub-agent on the appliance rather than spending the\npaid model's tokens on them. The appliance has no rate limit and no bill, so a\nlarge job is free there and expensive here. **The manager keeps the diagnosis,\nthe review and the final write** -- and \"the final write\" means the edits the\nsub-agent's own verification could not make trustworthy.\n\n**When you are curious about something, ask the author -- do not investigate it.**","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95803e3d-040d-4401-b98c-4ca7b716b706","uuid":"af34bf34-47cf-42d2-b4ba-e9a92fbcf9da","timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:02:53.016Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"13:# Tiiny Model Routing\n26:## When to Use\n52:## Prerequisites\n80:## The two halves\n98:## The lifecycle\n117:## Quick Reference\n119:### The tiers\n139:### The commands\n160:## Picking a model for a project role\n176:## Procedure\n178:### 1 -- Evaluate the job\n191:### 2 -- Pick the model, and check it can run\n206:### 3 -- Ensure the combination fits\n218:### 4 -- Reserve the device\n231:### 5 -- Load the batch's models\n245:### 6 -- Plan the work: the device is single-threaded\n274:### 7 -- Supervise the child\n289:### 8 -- Check the child's work\n298:### 9 -- Release the device\n315:### 10 -- Keep the catalogue honest\n334:## Thinking mode\n352:### The device knows more than a table does\n380:### \"Off\" means the cheapest available state\n387:### The label reports what happened, not what was asked\n404:### Thinking on needs a token floor\n423:## The image benefit\n448:## The lock\n468:## The required set\n544:## Scheduled work on the device\n552:### Pin a job to the box\n568:### The pin is what makes the saving real\n576:### Look for the provider block before you write one\n584:### Contention is decided by agent windows, not by the clock\n593:### The cron inactivity watchdog\n606:## Pitfalls\n909:## Delegating coding work\n915:### Two rules from the author that decide whether you delegate at all\n973:## Verification\n- **The package is the source; the installed directory is a copy.** The\n  backend, the controller and this skill are installed together into\n  `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` by `npx hermes-tiiny-router install`.\n  A hand edit there is a local edit: `doctor` reports it, and the next\n  `install` stops rather than overwrite it unless given `--force`. Make\n  lasting changes in the package and install again.\n- **This skill never downloads a model.** It chooses and loads from what is\n  already on the device.\n\n## Delegating coding work\n\nThe discipline for making the appliance do the writing and the manager\nagent do the judging. The full method is in\n[references/coding-delegation.md](references/coding-delegation.md).\n\n### Two rules from the author that decide whether you delegate at all\n\n**A multi-part job delegates; it does not get done inline.** When a task has\nseveral parts -- a sweep, a rewrite, a build, a set of independent edits -- hand\nthe mechanical parts to a sub-agent on the appliance rather than spending the\npaid model's tokens on them. The appliance has no rate limit and no bill, so a\nlarge job is free there and expensive here. **The manager keeps the diagnosis,\nthe review and the final write** -- and \"the final write\" means the edits the\nsub-agent's own verification could not make trustworthy.\n\n**When you are curious about something, ask the author -- do not investigate it.**","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_