{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFZpu5jJS3XCJYUsUiSi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] No doc or skill file references `~/.hermes/scripts/`, the Hermes source tree install path, the vault, or the sync script\n[x] No doc links to a path that does not exist in the repo\n[x] Every command shown in `README.md` exists in the package's CLI\n\nTicket 12 is done and committed in three commits. It was docs only, so I wrote no tests. Instead I checked it with a grep for the banned references and a script that resolves every markdown link; both came back clean. `npm test` (40 Node and 6 Python tests) and `test/test_register.py` still pass.\n\n1. **`README.md` (new).** It covers install, the config step (`--configure`, `--no-configure`, and printing the commands when there is no terminal), `doctor`, `route-check` and `ctl`, upgrading by running `install` again (with `--force` if files were edited), and `uninstall`. Every command it shows exists in `src/cli.ts`.\n2. **`AGENTS.md`.** The install steps now match the package install, and I added a short rule about em dashes and arrows in docs.\n3. **`SKILL.md` and `references/`.**\n   - All text about the vault, the sync script, symlinks, `~/.hermes/skills` and copying into the Hermes source tree is replaced: the package is the source, and you change it there and install again.\n   - Controller paths are written relative to `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`, or as `npx hermes-tiiny-router ctl` / `route-check`.\n   - I removed the mesh material, because `tiers.py` has no mesh URL support, so routing doesn't work with the mesh on its own. Running two boxes now uses each box's own HTTP start/stop calls instead of the mesh.\n   - `single-source-deployment.md` is deleted, and the two dead links are gone.\n4. **`docs/`.** Broken links are fixed and the checklist now uses `install` and `doctor`. Example goals that said \"under the vault\" now say \"in the notes folder\"; I checked that the router still classifies them as indexing.\n5. **Em dashes** are replaced with `--` outside code blocks in every file I touched.\n\nThings you may want to decide:\n- **`TIINY_VAULT` is still mentioned.** It's a real controller setting that points at the optional `hot.md` board, and renaming it is a code change outside this ticket.\n- **Some `→` arrows and em dashes remain on purpose.** They appear only where the docs quote text the code actually prints, such as the `off→low` and `code→generalist` route labels. Changing them would make the docs wrong about the output.\n- **Some stale content is untouched.** `docs/README.md` and `docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md` still describe the retired watchdog. A few personal setup details are also left (the Engraphis cron job, the OffGrid speech gateway). None of these were on the checklist.\n\nDetails are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1547,"cache_read_input_tokens":146958,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1547},"output_tokens":721,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95803e3d-040d-4401-b98c-4ca7b716b706","uuid":"432389b0-1c45-440d-bf57-e890e22da594","timestamp":"2026-11-21T06:03:16.192Z","request_id":"req_011ChFZptsantBpmHgn3RsiT"}
